  forbidden_inference A category-checked retained classified row -> current availability, a distinct buyer, a qualified provider or permission to contact.
  family external
  domain External / Source Accounting
  layer external
  semantic_question How many sources does this estate actually have, at which level -- publisher, protocol family, exact endpoint -- how much of that is the same thing listed twice, which of them a person has ever seen, and what is missing about each one?
  purpose The accounting plane between every inventory the estate holds and the small number of channels a page carries. It holds four levels -- SourceRoot (one publisher origin), ChannelFamily (one machine protocol at that root), Channel (one exact endpoint) and SourceGap (something unknown about that root) -- and keeps each inventory's provenance label on every root and channel it listed, so overlap is reported instead of totals being added. Channels are admitted only by the census (what the pages actually read), made active only by a page contribution receipt, and lowered into the estate's own HOT/WARM/COOL/COLD attention language. Its starvation report turns the estate against itself: which admitted channels never reach a person, which publisher or protocol dominates a surface, which discovery nobody examined.
  maturity implemented
  consumes InternetSource
  consumes ExternalEstateDensity
  consumes PublicEstatePassport
  publishes SourceChannel
  publishes SourceGap
