  witness scripts/tests/source_ledger_static_export_test.sh proves the Python-free exporter writes the bounded admitted index and two admitted source-profile leaves while withholding a candidate channel
  internal_calculus a convention is a question, not an observation: a feed lives at /feed, a catalogue at /data.json, an interface at /openapi.json, so a host nobody has ever linked can still be asked; anything found this way is protocol_derived_candidate and the host's robots policy still decides
  internal_calculus a host is asked for one catalogue, one feed and one interface and no more; past the first answer in a category the rest are the same estate said twice
  internal_calculus a host that answers nothing is remembered as asked, so the backlog is worked through rather than re-asked, and only those hosts are worth the one rendered second look that spends a credit
