  witness scripts/tests/firecrawl_second_look_test.mjs proves the rendered second look asks only previously silent hosts under read governance and a credential, emits only observed-link candidates, records denials, and stops on provider payment demand without marking unasked hosts or claiming measured billing
  witness 2026-09-19 twenty-one conventional addresses asked of hosts this estate had listed and never got a channel from: a first slice of 40 such hosts answered 13 times and produced 12 readable sources carrying 262 rows, against 650 addresses that did not answer and 101 that answered with nothing usable
  witness 2026-09-19 the page organ's existing JSON regime reads a DCAT, CKAN, Socrata or ArcGIS catalogue with no new reader: data.cityofchicago.org answered /data.json with 1,127 datasets, and three Socrata portals were admitted carrying 150 rows
  known_gap 27,152 roots in this ledger still have no channel of any state; the standing probe works through them a slice at a time, so the figure is a backlog being drawn down rather than a measurement of what those hosts publish
  known_gap the Bun/CUE ExternalEstate compatibility frontier accounting projection and native SourceFrontier C ledger still have distinct family and admission semantics; the mixed fixture proves Python-output compatibility, not typed parity with the native owner or whole-estate equivalence
  known_gap Clef and Clef-flash have a one-source live diagnostic witness, not a calibrated evaluation or a whole-estate run; Jev still lacks a Typesafe credential and remains an inactive alternate realization
  known_gap the rendered second look reaches hosts whose page only exists once a browser builds it, and is the one thing here that spends a metered credit on a host that has already said nothing once; it is bounded per pass rather than by a measured yield
  source_lineage 2026-09-17 the 40k+ target: count sources at the level they exist, and prove which of them a person ever sees
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tools/traktok_collect.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/traktok_collect.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/traktok_collect.test.mjs passes 12 tests and 98 assertions including 100000 synthetic observations, 300000 relationships, 1000 native shadow creator channels, short-page resumption, 64-bit IDs, stale leases, HTTP refusal, sealed Credentials, explicit refresh generations and verified retained read through BrowserHost
  invariant video observations, source-specific relations and collection checkpoints belong to SourceFrontier; individual posts do not become duplicate source channels
  invariant raw source bytes precede committed page advancement; bounded pages, lease checks, continuation IDs, retries and request budgets preserve resumability
  invariant a new explicit generation retains old observations; the same generation resumes without overwriting completed history
  invariant a collected read verifies page SHA-256, containment in the configured body owner, exact video membership and equality with the indexed record before producing the bounded browser projection
  invariant collector credentials remain inside the existing native Credentials apply boundary or process environment and are never retained in pages, state or receipts
  forbidden_inference a successful synthetic scale or installed-browser witness -> live TikTok access, real harvested posts or commercial reuse rights
  known_gap the configured ten-shard recipe query remains pending approved access with zero live posts; broad unofficial crawling and the full set of TraktoK research endpoints are not implemented

  invariant identity backfill joins a census source to a publisher QID only on evidence the estate holds, strongest first: the census channel's own root or channel identity, a host Wikidata records as an official website, or one label below such a host; a shared publishing host (FeedBurner, Megaphone, Substack, Blogspot and the like) never lends its own identity to what its tenants publish
  invariant a publisher name is backfilled only from the census root's real name or from retained items that all name one publisher; a QID placeholder used as a root name and a bare host in an item's publisher field are refused as names
  invariant every backfill row names its evidence and is stale-safe through the CMS owner, so a QID or name set since the cut is never overwritten; a source with no evidenced QID stays an IDENTITY gap and is routed to DISCOVER or HUMAN_VERIFY
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/source_frontier_test.sh proves the evidence ladder: news.nd.edu joins nd.edu's QID and keeps its CMS name, a FeedBurner-hosted show is refused, an agreed retained name is filled without a QID, a host-shaped name is refused, and a second CMS apply changes nothing
  witness 2026-10-30 on copies of the live estate (2,635 published sources, 1,514 missing a publisher QID or name) the backfill produced 47 rows: 31 QIDs one label below an official website, 16 names agreed by retained items; 140 platform-hosted sources and 178 host-shaped names were refused; applied to a CMS copy, sources with full publisher identity rose from 1,121 to 1,150 and retained-source identity gaps fell from 1,359 to 1,338
  forbidden_inference a host one label below an organization's official website -> that organization authored, endorsed or controls every item the source carries
  forbidden_inference a backfilled publisher identity -> an account, membership, partnership or authority for that publisher anywhere in Aurekai
  known_gap 1,483 of the 1,514 sources missing identity have no QID evidence held locally; Wikidata's newspaper, magazine, radio and television classes were refused by rate limit in the original harvest, so closing them needs a governed DISCOVER pass
interaction source-frontier-allocates-page-sources
  source source-frontier
  destination page-composition
  relation allocates_admitted_channels
  preserves each channel's census row, the publisher it belongs to and when it last reached a person
  drops inventory labels, gaps, attention levels and every channel the census has not admitted
  forbidden_inference a page's choice of sources -> a ranking of those sources by quality, truth or importance
  invalidates_on census admissions, contribution receipts, the ledger's absence (the declared families still fill the page)
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_programs_test.sh

interaction source-frontier-exports-admitted-ledger
  source source-frontier
  destination web-address-edge
  relation compiles_admitted_source_coordinates
  preserves exact admitted channel address and its bounded index position
  drops candidate, eligible, waiting-credential and virtual-only channels
  forbidden_inference an exported source profile -> an active public program contribution, current endpoint reachability, or publisher endorsement
  invalidates_on census admission state or exact channel address
  witness scripts/tests/source_ledger_static_export_test.sh

interaction source-frontier-reads-census-admissions
  source internet-census
  destination source-frontier
  relation admits_channels
  preserves the exact published address, its family as the channel's material and the credential it waits for
  drops unpublished rows, retained bodies and every item the census read
  forbidden_inference an admitted channel -> a lawful right to read it again, or its content being current
  invalidates_on census publication, credential state
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/source_frontier_test.sh

interaction source-frontier-collection-native-credentials
  source source-frontier
  destination credential-boundary
  relation projects_as
  preserves sealed provider authorization, fixed destination and source-specific access requirements
  binding cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tools/traktok_collect.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/traktok_collect.test.mjs
  forbidden_inference configured credentials -> approved access or current remote success

interaction source-frontier-retained-post-browser
  source source-frontier
  destination browser-host
  relation projects_as
  preserves exact collection and post, verified retained source bytes, observation time and source-specific standing
  binding integrations/browser/host/bonfyre-browser-host.mjs
  witness integrations/browser/tests/workbench-live.test.mjs
  forbidden_inference a retained post read -> a live page fetch or publication permission

interaction foreign-observation-to-discourse-review
  source foreign-twin
  destination source-frontier
  relation decodes_retained_observation
  preserves public source URL, SHA-256, receipt path and time, exact topic/post identity, original-poster updates and uncovered stream IDs
  drops applicant post bodies from the original-poster projection, executable interpretation of HTML and inference of job availability
  binding cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/src/main.c discourse-review
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/discourse_thread.test.mjs
  forbidden_inference a source-backed reading plan -> permission to contact or an automatically qualified sales opportunity

interaction source-frontier-backfills-census-identity
  source source-frontier
  destination internet-census
  relation proposes_publisher_identity
  preserves the census row id and namespace, the QID or name, the evidence that supports it and the empty-field condition the CMS owner checks before writing
  drops sources with conflicting, ambiguous or platform-borrowed identity and every name that is only a host
  forbidden_inference a proposed identity row -> a written CMS fact; only the CMS owner applies it, and only where the field is still empty
  invalidates_on census publication, root identity, retained item publishers
  witness cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tests/source_frontier_test.sh
